<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Typd's entitlements, signed into the app and its helpers by scripts/after-pack.js and into the
  update package's app by scripts/app-update-package.js (docs/MAC.md "Code signing").

  com.apple.security.device.audio-input: the microphone. macOS enforces it only under the hardened
  runtime; with it, a missing one makes macOS refuse the microphone with no prompt and no entry in
  Privacy & Security (checked in CI: a hardened build without it was refused at once on macOS 14, 15,
  26 and 27). The Mac CI checks it is in every bundle.

  From 0.2.13 the Developer ID build (TYPD_MAC_SIGN_DEVID=1) runs under the hardened runtime, which
  notarization requires, so it also needs:
  - com.apple.security.automation.apple-events: pasting and reading a selection go through Apple
    events (osascript, on Typd's behalf); the hardened runtime blocks them without it.
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory: V8, in Electron's main and
    helper processes.
  The self-signed build has no hardened runtime, so these change nothing there. Entitlements are not
  part of the designated requirement.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
